WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:01.930
My name's Tim.

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:04.430
I'm the principal rural fire officer for the
district.

00:00:04.430 --> 00:00:06.190
Waimakariri District that is.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:10.610
The fire season is finally heating up after
a wet spring.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:15.339
Under these hot, dry, windy conditions it's
very easy for a fire to get out of control.

00:00:15.339 --> 00:00:19.910
If you are found responsible for a fire such as this, you could well be held liable and

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.710
wear the costs of containing and extinguishing that fire.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:24.919
So please, think before light.

00:00:24.919 --> 00:00:29.859
Here are some tips, that you might think about
before you light a fire.

00:00:29.859 --> 00:00:34.000
The Waimakariri District is now under a restricted
fire season.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.520
This means that no fires in the open are to
be lit without a permit.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.150
Check out the video linked below for more
information.

00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:44.900
If you're on a lifestyle block or farm, check
the weather forecast before lighting.

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:50.980
Far too many fires last year were foolishly
started when strong winds were predicted.

00:00:50.980 --> 00:00:54.680
Keep a hose nearby, charged and ready for
immediate use.

00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:59.150
And keep ten to thirty metres clearance around
buildings and outhouses.

00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:02.850
Remember the more you feed it, the bigger
a fire grows.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:07.300
Don't mess around with fire, because when
it gets out of control, things go very bad,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:08.650
very fast.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:12.370
Just because it's no longer smoking, it doesn't
mean it's out.

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:17.050
Fires can smoulder for months, so before leaving,
check by putting your hand in the ashes.

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:22.200
If the ashes are still warm, open it up, put
a hose in it and wet it down thoroughly.

00:01:22.220 --> 00:01:27.560
We don't want a repeat of previous year's
mistakes,  so to ensure we all have a great summer

00:01:27.560 --> 00:01:30.330
please, think before you light.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:35.710
For more information about the restricted
fire season and applying for a permit, please

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:39.170
visit waimakariri.govt.nz

